From 50c0cbe3ee47bc94643865bbd4d0339f2ab6e024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:44:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: the HDR10+ InfoFrame of each picture, from its
 own metadata

A picture of an HDR10+ stream carries its dynamic metadata (SMPTE ST 2094-40,
which FFmpeg reads from the ITU-T T.35 message of each HEVC and AV1 picture:
AV_FRAME_DATA_DYNAMIC_HDR_PLUS). Kodi only marked the stream as HDR10+, and
nothing could send the metadata: the display got HDR10 only.

The decoders (FFmpeg and DRM PRIME) now give each picture the payload of
its HDR10+ vendor-specific InfoFrame (VideoPicture::hdr10PlusVsif), built
from the picture's own metadata by utils/HDR10PlusVsif.h; a picture without
HDR10+ metadata has none. The InfoFrame is defined by the HDR10+
specification, which HDR10+ Technologies gives only to its adopters; the
layout and the coding of each field are those of the GPL code CoreELEC
sends it with (Amlogic's common_drivers), read as data. A host test checks
them against the metadata of FFmpeg's FATE test, read back from T.35 as a
decoder reads it.
